 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How a news item is put together",
     "texto": [
      "To read a short news item, look for **when**, **where**, **what happened**, **who was affected**, the cause and the consequences. Not all of these details always appear, nor in the same order: the headline and the opening usually highlight the most important thing.",
      "The source can appear with **theo…** (\"according to…\") or **…cho biết** (\"…reported that…\"): «Theo cảnh sát…» / «Một nhân chứng cho biết…». Notice who provides the information.",
      "If a fact isn't known yet, you may find «**Nguyên nhân đang được điều tra**» (the cause is being investigated) or «**Chưa rõ…**» (it isn't yet clear…).",
      "The three news items in this activity are fictional and were written for practice; they don't describe documented events."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Approximate figures",
     "texto": [
      "**khoảng** = about, around. **gần** = nearly. **hơn** = more than. **dưới** = less than. **ít nhất** = at least. **hàng** + chục / trăm / nghìn = tens / hundreds / thousands of: «**hàng trăm** người» = hundreds of people.",
      "They go **before** the number: «**hơn** ba mươi người», «**gần** hai tiếng»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
